# T-997: Reverse functional dependency resolution (type-system-health-s841-followup)
# Verifies that a class with FD (src) → (dst) and injective: true parses and
# typechecks without error.
#
# What this test covers:
#   - Class declaration syntax with multi-parameter type variables
#   - FD annotation: determines: [[[src] dst]] with resolver and injective fields
#   - The type checker accepts the class declaration without error
#   - A program using only the class declaration (no instance or call-site) evaluates correctly
[
  # Coercible class with FD: src determines dst (injective resolver)
  Coercible: [class [let Coercible src dst]
    [determines: [[[src] dst]]  resolver: CoercibleResolver  injective: 1]
    coerce: [Fn@dst [src]]]

  # Prove the class declaration was accepted: return a simple value
  result: 42
]

---

%.result
=== out
Int(42)
